## Why This Is Asked

This question probes offline-first UX, syncing, and conflict resolution with Realm Sync and MongoDB Atlas in a real-world CAD-like workflow.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first data modeling with Realm
- Sync strategies and optimistic UI
- Conflict resolution using per-annotation versioning and vector-merge
- Audit trails and crash-safe resume

## Code Example

```swift
class Annotation: Object {
  @objc dynamic var id = UUID().uuidString
  @objc dynamic var blueprintId = ""
  @objc dynamic var drawingData = Data()
  @objc dynamic var note: String? = nil
  @objc dynamic var color = "black"
  @objc dynamic var stroke: Double = 1.0
  @objc dynamic var createdAt = Date()
  @objc dynamic var updatedAt = Date()
  @objc dynamic var authorId = ""
  @objc dynamic var version = 0
  override static func primaryKey() -> String? { return "id" }
}
```

